{
 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "In nineteen eighty-six, one man scored the dirtiest goal and the most beautiful goal in World Cup history, four minutes apart.",
   "s": 0.08,
   "e": 6.423
  },
  {
   "text": "He grew up on the dirt roads of Villa Fiorito, outside Buenos Aires, and slept hugging his first football.",
   "s": 6.494,
   "e": 12.252
  },
  {
   "text": "At twenty-five, he's Argentina's captain in a quarter-final against England, in front of a hundred and fourteen thousand people in Mexico City.",
   "s": 12.322,
   "e": 19.777
  },
  {
   "text": "Six minutes into the second half, the ball floats up toward the English goalkeeper, who is twenty centimetres taller.",
   "s": 19.847,
   "e": 25.603
  },
  {
   "text": "Maradona jumps anyway, and punches it into the net with his left hand.",
   "s": 25.673,
   "e": 29.151
  },
  {
   "text": "Luckily for Argentina, the referee didn't see a thing.",
   "s": 29.221,
   "e": 31.864
  },
  {
   "text": "Unluckily for England, Maradona was about to use his feet.",
   "s": 31.934,
   "e": 34.878
  },
  {
   "text": "Four minutes later, he picks up the ball in his own half, and just starts running.",
   "s": 34.948,
   "e": 38.657
  },
  {
   "text": "One Englishman, two, three, four, then the goalkeeper. Sixty metres, in about ten seconds.",
   "s": 38.727,
   "e": 43.22
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, Maradona was only one metre sixty-five, with his weight low to the ground.",
   "s": 43.29,
   "e": 47.474
  },
  {
   "text": "Ever watched a waiter carry a tall stack of plates? He takes every corner slowly. A short stack can whip around without tipping.",
   "s": 47.544,
   "e": 53.968
  },
  {
   "text": "Argentina went on to win the whole World Cup.",
   "s": 54.038,
   "e": 56.173
  },
  {
   "text": "And to this day, half the world remembers that match for his hand, and the other half for his feet.",
   "s": 56.243,
   "e": 60.686
  }
 ],
